Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array

originally a sorted array and it is rotated between 1 to n times

so if the original array was nums=[1,2,3,4,5,6]

if rotated 1 times

[6,7,1,2,3,4,5]

if rotated 4 times

[3,4,5,6,1,2]

if 6 times as the length of nums

[3,4,5,6,7,1,2]
it will be back to original

we have to find the minimum element in this array

Instead of solving the question is O(n) we have to solve it in O(logn) using binary search

So the deduced problem statement is, as we have rotated the sorted array, creating two sorted array which are separated by a point and that point is the minimum point

now we will define low as 0 and high as length of nums -1

and then we will go to the next part of using the binary search for the same

if the mid value of the array is higher than the rightmost high value that means the minimum point is on the right side

whereas if the mid value of the array is lower than the rightmost high value that means the minimum point is on the left side

also the mid point itself can be the minimum value as we will use Math.min on the solution and the nums[mid] value to keep getting the lowest value in the array
